WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.888
Deploying is a post of the file to the
detection rules endpoint, then a read-back.

2
00:00:04.888 --> 00:00:09.776
Validation is an export of everything
deployed, compared with the repository.

3
00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:14.167
The guide's pass: every rule in the
repository is deployed with the same

4
00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:18.787
query text and status, and nothing is
deployed that isn't in the repository.

5
00:00:18.787 --> 00:00:20.401
Now the government clouds.

6
00:00:20.401 --> 00:00:26.036
Microsoft Learn's run hunting query page
has a national-cloud table: available

7
00:00:26.036 --> 00:00:31.238
on the global service, which G C C uses,
and in U S Government L four and L five.

8
00:00:31.238 --> 00:00:34.897
Learn's detection rules pages
have no national-cloud table,

9
00:00:34.897 --> 00:00:39.975
so the guide records the A P I's government-cloud
availability as not yet specified,

10
00:00:39.975 --> 00:00:42.888
and lists it among the
things it couldn't verify.

11
00:00:42.888 --> 00:00:46.247
The interim path in G C C
High and D O D is to create

12
00:00:46.247 --> 00:00:49.950
the rule in the portal from
the same repository file.

13
00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:52.459
The file stays the source
of truth either way,

14
00:00:52.459 --> 00:00:55.440
and the deployed-rules check
still compares the two.
